# Email addresses matching any of the patterns below cannot be used to register
# an account. Matching is case-insensitive; blank lines and lines starting with
# '#' are ignored. Patterns are shell-style globs (fnmatch), not regexes:
#
#   *       matches any sequence of characters (including '@' and '.')
#   ?       matches any single character
#   [seq]   matches any character in seq
#   [!seq]  matches any character not in seq
#
# A pattern starting with '!' is an exception: if it matches, the address is not
# blocked. Lines are processed top to bottom and the first match decides, so
# exceptions must be listed before the pattern they carve out.
#
# The file is read on every registration attempt, so changes take effect without
# a restart. It is mounted into the gatekeeper container by directory (not by
# file), so replacing it (as editors, sed -i and git do) works as well as editing
# it in place; the container path is fixed at /etc/gatekeeper/email-blocklist.txt.
#
# Examples:
#
#   !smith+ok@gmail.com
#   *@outlook.com
#   *@*.foobar.example
#   smith+*@gmail.com
